WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:01.789
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.969
In this lesson, we will turn defects into accountable repairs.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.069
A defect reported in chat can be forgotten when it has no work order, owner,

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.550
approval, or return-to-service record.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:17.059
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:19.030
practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.869
A failed pump test creates a work order, and the engine stays on a safety

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:25.949
hold until the repair is approved.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:30.099
Turn a failed check or reported defect into a tracked repair and

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:32.000
a documented return to service.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.900
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.150
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:38.779 --> 00:00:39.670
Work Orders.

00:00:40.029 --> 00:00:41.940
Repair and maintenance work orders.

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:45.759
Create work orders from failed checks or reported defects.

00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:49.689
Availability also depends on Maintenance, Readiness Pro.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.130
Check access in the target department.

00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:54.150
Preventive maintenance.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.099
Recurring maintenance schedules.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.300
Schedule routine service for each apparatus.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.329
Availability also depends on Readiness Pro, Maintenance.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.909
Check access in the target department.

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:08.459
Maintenance policies and approvals.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.110
Repair approvals and safety holds.

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:15.089
Decide who approves repairs and returns equipment to service.

00:01:15.559 --> 00:01:19.120
Availability also depends on Readiness Pro, Maintenance.

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:21.559
Check access in the target department.

00:01:22.289 --> 00:01:23.330
New Work Order.

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:24.849
Open a work order.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.130
Requires the Readiness Pro add-on.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.579
Checklists remain available without it.

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:33.319
Availability also depends on Maintenance, Readiness Pro.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.840
Check access in the target department.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:38.309
Maintenance history and reports.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.030
Maintenance history, repair costs and safety holds.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.390
Requires the Readiness Pro add-on.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.980
Checklists remain available without it.

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:50.900
Availability also depends on Readiness Pro, Maintenance.

00:01:51.289 --> 00:01:53.339
Check access in the target department.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:54.940
Readiness Pro.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.310
The Readiness Pro add-on: work orders, preventive maintenance,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.700
repair approvals and safety holds.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:04.300
Checklists do not require this add-on.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.370
Maintenance needs its module, permissions and active entitlement.

00:02:08.859 --> 00:02:12.570
Historical evidence and hold release follow owning-module rules.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.579
Availability also depends on Readiness Pro.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.900
Check access in the target department.

00:02:18.619 --> 00:02:23.190
Work-order operations connect parts, vendor charges, approval requests,

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.360
and spending policy to a repair.

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:30.669
Review policy, reserve a sample part, record its movement and a vendor charge,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.860
then request the required approval.

00:02:33.339 --> 00:02:37.549
Reconcile repair cost and part movement with the work order and approval decision.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.850
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.250
recording the live workflow.

00:02:43.009 --> 00:02:46.380
Bulk maintenance tools preview imported rows or assignment

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.089
changes before applying them.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.719
Use the import template or select demo rows, preview the proposed

00:02:52.719 --> 00:02:55.039
changes, and review the row outcomes.

00:02:55.409 --> 00:02:59.050
Confirm the preview, current revisions, and the observed result

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.909
after an authorized demo apply.

00:03:01.339 --> 00:03:04.089
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:03:04.089 --> 00:03:05.610
recording the live workflow.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.019
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.150
Step 1.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:14.869
Confirm Readiness Pro access, the Maintenance module, and permissions.

00:03:15.289 --> 00:03:15.980
Step 2.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:20.419
Create a work order from a reported defect and assign responsibility.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:21.570
Step 3.

00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:25.159
Record corrective work and follow the configured approval

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:26.639
and safety-hold process.

00:03:27.229 --> 00:03:28.709
Now verify the result.

00:03:29.199 --> 00:03:34.309
Review the repair history, recorded costs, approval state, and any safety hold.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.290
Release follows the owning maintenance workflow.

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:40.990
A common problem to watch for: Checklists are available

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.650
separately from Readiness Pro.

00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:47.530
Buying maintenance access does not configure the module or approval policy.

00:03:48.179 --> 00:03:49.740
Your practice task is simple.

00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:54.710
Track a demo pump-test defect through assignment, repair, review,

00:03:54.909 --> 00:03:56.819
and documented return to service.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.269
Measure unresolved work-order age.

00:03:59.649 --> 00:04:03.489
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

